From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 16:10:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Guard browser packet drain before server start

The browser frame hook moved packet draining outside the native wait loop
but dropped its com_sv_running guard. At the main menu svs.clients is NULL;
the download queue walks unallocated client state and traps in MSG_WriteData.
Preserve the native guard for both SP and MP while keeping nonblocking drain.

diff --git a/SP/code/qcommon/common.c b/SP/code/qcommon/common.c
--- a/SP/code/qcommon/common.c
+++ b/SP/code/qcommon/common.c
@@ -2814,7 +2814,9 @@
 	// Native builds drain fragmented netchan messages while waiting for the
 	// next frame.  A browser main loop must never block, so service the same
 	// queue once per animation frame instead.
-	SV_SendQueuedPackets();
+	if ( com_sv_running->integer ) {
+		SV_SendQueuedPackets();
+	}
 #endif
 
 	// if "dedicated" has been modified, start up
diff --git a/MP/code/qcommon/common.c b/MP/code/qcommon/common.c
--- a/MP/code/qcommon/common.c
+++ b/MP/code/qcommon/common.c
@@ -3272,7 +3272,9 @@
 	// Native builds drain fragmented netchan messages while waiting for the
 	// next frame.  A browser main loop must never block, so service the same
 	// queue once per animation frame instead.
-	SV_SendQueuedPackets();
+	if ( com_sv_running->integer ) {
+		SV_SendQueuedPackets();
+	}
 #endif
 
 	// if "dedicated" has been modified, start up
